"""Pool of sample protein sequences served by the "random sequence" chip.

Edit ``SAMPLE_SEQUENCES`` to add, remove, or tweak the entries offered to the
user — each click of the chip picks one record at random. A record needs:

* ``label``      — short human-readable name shown nowhere by default, handy
                   when you scan this file.
* ``accession``  — UniProt accession, kept for reference.
* ``question``   — the question appended after the sequence in the chat.
* ``sequence``   — the amino-acid sequence as a single uppercase string
                   (no FASTA header, no line breaks).

All sequences below are canonical human UniProt entries.
"""

